[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2783915657","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105110#issuecomment-2783915657","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105110","id":2783915657,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6l7y6J","user":{"login":"SRowick","id":42491371,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyNDkxMzcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42491371?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SRowick","html_url":"https://github.com/SRowick","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SRowick/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SRowick/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SRowick/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SRowick/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SRowick/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SRowick/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SRowick/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SRowick/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SRowick/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-07T16:20:10Z","updated_at":"2025-04-07T16:20:10Z","body":"I think it might also be helpful to note that this worked as desired in a [Godot 2.1 example project](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-demo-projects/tree/2.1/2d/isometric_light)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2783915657/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2830388489","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105110#issuecomment-2830388489","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105110","id":2830388489,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6otE0J","user":{"login":"KerekesDavid","id":9087461,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwODc0NjE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9087461?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid","html_url":"https://github.com/KerekesDavid","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-25T13:09:16Z","updated_at":"2025-04-25T13:09:16Z","body":"I fond the exact same workaround, and have the same problem with it in a top-down 2D situation. I just ended up playing with the light radius until the effect is not really visible anymore, but if you find an actual fix to this let me know :)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2830388489/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3148330044","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105110#issuecomment-3148330044","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105110","id":3148330044,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc67p7Q8","user":{"login":"ThompZon","id":2388527,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzODg1Mjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2388527?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThompZon","html_url":"https://github.com/ThompZon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThompZon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThompZon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThompZon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThompZon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThompZon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThompZon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThompZon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThompZon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThompZon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-03T10:37:59Z","updated_at":"2025-08-03T10:37:59Z","body":"Imo, the problem is not only that the occluders cast shadows on the tile itself, it must also handle adjacent occluders or it will cause unexpected results (See 2nd image). \n\n1st image:\n<img width=\"244\" height=\"243\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e014fae4-0c29-46ca-b6c7-79730b7bc33b\" />\nDoing the method in original post (using 2 light mask layers where the wall receives lights from one and the floor shadow is on the other), I can manage result like 1st image\n\n2nd image:\n<img width=\"143\" height=\"157\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a41a4915-9b6b-4a9b-a212-dbd8e7013539\" />\nBy using only one lightmask layer and instead tweaking the Wall TileMapLayer's TileSet's Occluder's Polygon Cull Mode to CounterClockWise, I can get a result like the 2nd image. Note that this is basically a way to get the occluder NOT to cast shadow on itself (only works in top-down 2D, not in isometric example!). \n\nMy best attempt at formulating a \"feature\" or \"setting\" to solve this is for both cases: \n\"If tile get light directly from a source, keep it for the entire tile but occlude for anything after, ignoring occluders from adjacent tiles with this setting that also receives light directly from the source\". Maybe it's possible to say this in an easier way. \n\nI can see how this can seem like niche problem, but if you want a 2d game with walls that light up \"as you expect\", this is needed imo. I was very surprised that this was basically impossible to solve using the built in lightning system.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3148330044/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]